1. Definitions and scope

"Original Material" means the MusicSync code, documentation, build scripts,
and other material whose rights holder applies this license, including the
MusicSyncCore package. Independently licensed third-party material is excluded.

"Covered Project" means the Original Material, its modifications, and the
software project that incorporates any copyright-protected portion of it by
copying, embedding, compiling, or linking that portion into a program. This
includes the combined program's application-specific modules, not merely the
copied MusicSync files. Independent programs that only communicate through
ordinary network protocols, independent works in an aggregate distribution,
and System Dependencies are excluded.

"System Dependencies" means independently licensed operating systems, SDKs,
compilers, runtimes, standard system libraries, and unmodified independently
licensed third-party packages. Their own licenses continue to apply; this
license does not require relicensing them or disclosing their proprietary
source. Their identity, version, license, and public acquisition instructions
must be documented when needed to build the Covered Project. If a dependency
cannot lawfully be combined with these terms, this license does not grant
permission to distribute that combination.

"Corresponding Source" means the complete, unobfuscated preferred form for
modifying the Covered Project, including application-specific source modules,
modifications, project files, dependency/version declarations, and scripts and
instructions needed to build, install, and run the distributed or served
version. A patch alone, interface stubs, minified/generated output without its
editable source, or only the reused MusicSync files is not sufficient. Private
keys, signing certificates, account credentials, personal data, and System
Dependencies need not be disclosed. Document how a user supplies their own
credentials or uses an unsigned build where applicable.

"NonCommercial" means not primarily intended for or directed toward commercial
advantage or monetary compensation. Being a nonprofit organization, or offering
an app without an upfront price, does not by itself make a use NonCommercial.
Paid products, paid access, advertising-funded products, and commercial services
incorporating the Original Material are not permitted under this license.

