3. Attribution and notices

When sharing the Original Material, code excerpts, or a Covered Project:

(a) preserve supplied author/copyright notices and this license;
(b) identify MusicSync and ACOPS1206, link to the original repository where
    reasonably practicable, and identify this license;
(c) identify your modifications and their author without implying endorsement;
(d) include LICENSE and NOTICE with source and binary distributions; and
(e) make the attribution reasonably accessible to users of distributed apps or
    services, for example in About, Help, Credits, or accompanying documentation.

For a publicly shared code excerpt, place the attribution alongside the excerpt
or in the containing document's clearly identified credits. Reasonable formats
are allowed; a particular visual design or exact sentence is not mandatory.
The attribution example in NOTICE may be used. Warranty disclaimers must remain.

4. Public source sharing and reciprocal licensing

If you distribute a Covered Project in source or binary form, or allow users
other than yourself to interact with it over a network, you must, no later than
that distribution or availability:

(a) publish its complete Corresponding Source at a publicly accessible download
    URL or public source repository, without payment, login, or a nondisclosure
    agreement; identify the exact source revision matching each version;
(b) include a prominent, working source link in the application/service or its
    accompanying documentation, and give that link to recipients;
(c) license your application-specific contributions to that Covered Project
    under this same license, and preserve recipients' rights to access, modify,
    and redistribute it for NonCommercial purposes; and
(d) keep that source available while you distribute or serve the version and
    for at least three years after you last distribute or serve it. Recipients
    may archive and redistribute that source under this license.

Do not publish, serve, or distribute a Covered Project if you lack authority to
meet these obligations for its application-specific source. You may not conceal
that source in a proprietary linked module to avoid this section, replace this
license with a closed-source license for a Covered Project, or impose terms or
technical measures that prevent the granted NonCommercial rights. Separately
licensed System Dependencies and independent programs retain their licenses.

